clean_summary:
We've been using iPhUMI for MuSE/UMI-FT. The iPhone version is a significant upgrade from the original UMI design, with better slam and a more user-friendly interface.

@austinapatel: "We are also excited to release iPhUMI ('eye-foo-me'). It addresses localization challenges with the GoPro UMI, enabling rapid data collection across diverse environments and tasks. During deployment, iPhUMI allows you to command your robot via demonstration."

The GitHub repository provides a handheld data collection interface for training visuomotor robot manipulation policies and a hardware interface for behavior prompting.

I couldn’t make it to RSS this year, but Jeannette @leto__jean will be presenting HoMMI on behalf of our team today (7/16) at 3:15pm in the Imitation Learning 3 session and the poster session.

If you’re in Sydney, come check it out!

@XiaomengXu11: "Can we learn whole-body mobile manipulation directly from human demonstrations? Introducing Whole-Body Mobile Manipulation Interface (HoMMI). Egocentric + UMI, 0 teleop, bimanual and whole-body manipulation, long-horizon navigation, active perception."

Check out the @dingmyu and the team's amazing website to get the build details on how to build your own Handroid.

@dingmyu: "🤖 A robot that transforms between humanoid and dexterous hand? Introducing Handroid, a reconfigurable robot with a shared 27-DoF body. The same joints serve different roles, expanding the robot's task space with shared sensing and control interfaces."

A video demonstrates Handroid's ability to reconfigure between a humanoid form and a dexterous hand, showcasing its versatility in movement and function.
